@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 ### Added
 
+- When a background subagent resolves its model, the spawning agent now gets a hidden message naming it, such as ``Subagent `fable` started on `provider/model` (thinking level low).`` It is sent again if the subagent moves to another model. Before this the agent had only the name it gave the worker and could take it for a different model.
 - Added the `retry.accountMode` setting (`sequential` by default, or `balanced`). With `sequential`, Anthropic accounts are used one at a time: every session and subagent follows the account that served last until it is blocked or spent, then moves to the next.
 - New `usage_bar` status-line segment, in the `default` preset right after the context percent: a five-cell progress bar, the percent used and the window tag (`━━━━━ 100% 7d`) for the active account. New `statusLine.usageWindow` setting (`weekly` by default, `session`, `worst`) chooses the 7 Day window, the 5 Hour window or the more used one. For a Claude model with its own weekly counter (Fable, Mythos, Opus, Sonnet) `weekly` uses the more used of the shared and the model's 7 Day row, tagged `7d fable`; a provider without a 7 Day window draws no bar in `weekly` mode, and `session` falls back to its shortest window under its own tag. It renders nothing when the provider reports no usage windows, or when several accounts have no resolved one.
 - When a provider holds two or more stored OAuth accounts, the status line names the session's account in the model: `Anthropic (B) > Sonnet 5.5`, and the footer's raw model id reads `anthropic-b/claude-sonnet-5-5`. The letter is the account's position in `omp usage accounts` order (A first) and follows an account change mid-session. Single-account providers look as before.
